# Bytes of RAM the linker keeps below the initial stack pointer for the call
# stack (`STACK_RESERVE` in the link script; the SDK's default is 32768).
# The first number is the reserve. It must hold the deepest stack the shipped
# game reaches plus a 25% margin, rounded up to 1 KiB:
# `cargo hl-build stack` replays the shipped disc on maps through the title menu
# and fails when a watermark comes within that margin, and it relinks the
# shipping image as an ELF and bounds every call chain statically (recursion
# taken to the depth of the campaign's deepest BSP trees, c2a4a: 84 levels of
# 136 B). The static bound is the one that sets this number: 19,664 B on
# 2026-10-15, so 19,664 * 1.25 = 24,580 rounds up to 25 KiB. The emulator
# watermark over the campaign maps is about 10 KB, but a trace down the deepest
# tree nests 85 frames, which no walk is certain to hit.
# HLPSX_STACK_RESERVE overrides it for a build that is only profiled.
25600
